    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** serving as our clear offensive anchor. With an elite score of 82.12, he benefits significantly from his leadoff spot against Reynaldo L\u00f3pez, combined with a strong 0.371 xwOBA that gives him a high floor for runs and a ceiling for steals. **Lars Nootbaar** follows closely behind with a 67.77 rating; he is well-positioned to capitalize on a favorable platoon edge against Sandy Alcantara, while **Colt Keith** (61.14) rounds out our top-tier plays by securing the #3 spot against Jos\u00e9 Soriano, where his strong plate discipline and park factors allow him to transcend the moderate xERA of his opponent.\n\nManaging the volatility of the back-end spots remains critical, as **Carson Benge** (57.53), **Kazuma Okamoto** (57.36), and **Josh Smith** (57.17) provide stable, if marginal, output. The most difficult decision rested on the bench, where **Chase Meidroth** (36.45) just missed the cut. While his underlying metrics are decent, the optimizer ultimately pivoted away from him due to a poor matchup against Gavin Williams (2.89 xERA), whose elite skill effectively neutralized **Chase Meidroth**\u2019s utility for today. Similarly, **Hector Rodriguez** faced a difficult assignment against Tarik Skubal, forcing us to bench him to protect our games-played caps.\n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" status across the board, particularly with **Dillon Dingler** (42.79) and **Pedro Ramirez** (49.02). Both sit in the bottom tier of our starters; if these players are bumped down in the order or removed from the starting lineup entirely, we will need to pivot immediately to prevent empty production. Given that stolen bases remain our scarcest category, **Josh Smith**\u2019s 60% SB-hold probability remains a vital, albeit high-risk, component of his projection. We are proceeding with the current configuration, monitoring weather and late-scratches as we look to maximize efficiency in the final stretch of the season.",
